<title>USA: U.S. NAPM index 51.7 in Sept versus 52.6 in Aug.</title>
<headline>U.S. NAPM index 51.7 in Sept versus 52.6 in Aug.</headline>
<dateline>TEMPE, Ariz. 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Association of Purchasing Management (NAPM) said on Tuesday its index of manufacturing activity fell to 51.7 in September from 52.6 in August. A listing of the main NAPM components follows:</p>
<p>		   Sept  Aug   July  June  May  April  March  Feb</p>
<p>PMI		51.7  52.6  50.2  54.3  49.3  50.1  46.9  45.2</p>
<p>Production     54.1  57.0  52.4  55.4  52.7  52.1  46.6  44.0</p>
<p>New Orders     56.3  55.6  54.0  61.3  52.4  53.8  49.7  44.7</p>
<p>Supplier Deliv 49.7  52.5  50.9  53.2  50.0  49.2  49.9  50.1</p>
<p>Inventories    44.8  41.6  41.2  42.3  38.3  44.6  38.8  43.9</p>
<p>Employment     46.9  48.2  45.5  49.4  45.5  45.3  44.7  44.3</p>
<p>Prices	   51.2  47.4  44.5  49.0  50.8  40.1  39.5  38.3</p>
<p>Export Orders  56.8  57.2  53.8  53.9  56.9  51.4  50.4  49.4</p>
<p>Imports	  51.8  50.6  53.7  48.6  49.8  46.2  46.3  47.6</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
